## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure Policy and how to implement guardrails that cover new and existing resources, plus rollout and rollback planning.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy and Initiatives
- Deny vs DeployIfNotExists vs AuditIfNotExists
- Storage Account security controls (public access, HTTPS, encryption)
- Tag-based governance and rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/publicAccess", "notEquals": "None" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts.enableHttpsTrafficOnly", "notEquals": true },
        { "field": "tags.env", "exists": false }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  },
  "parameters": {}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle existing storage accounts that violate these rules during rollout?
- What metrics and alerts would you configure to monitor policy compliance over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply core Azure security controls (network, identities, policy) in a concrete, beginner-friendly scenario. It emphasizes least privilege, auditable changes, and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and DENY public access for storage/sql
- User-Assigned Managed Identities for service-to-resource access
- Azure Policy to enforce private endpoints and deny public exposure
- Canary rollout and quick rollback plan with policy reversion

## Code Example
```json
// Policy (simplified) to deny public network access on storage and SQL
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Sql/servers"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify private endpoints are in effect across all resources?
- What tests ensure rollback can restore previous connectivity without downtime?
